               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 52-year-old female, admitted on 17/10/2007 with acute lower abdominal pain and suspected tubal pregnancy. On admission, physical examination, transvaginal ultrasound, and serum beta-hCG confirmed a right-sided tubal ectopic pregnancy without signs of rupture. Given the patient's hemodynamic stability, laparoscopic evaluation was performed, revealing an intact tubal ectopic pregnancy. A laparoscopic salpingectomy was carried out successfully with no intraoperative complications. Postoperative recovery was uneventful. Wound care was provided and vital signs remained stable throughout the stay. The patient was discharged home on 23/10/2007 in good general condition. Follow-up beta-hCG monitoring and outpatient review in six weeks are recommended. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you have any questions.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
